window.ENGLISH_CLASSICS = {"updatedAt":"2026-10-07","source":{"url":"https://www.lyg.gov.cn/zglygzfmhwz/fwzx_jywh/content/3513b8fd-35eb-497e-b1b1-3288a4b37da3.html","title":"连云港市中小学“真阅读工程”推荐书目（2026年修订）","publishedAt":"2026-06-15","documentDate":"2026-05-14","term":"第一学期","status":"市级推荐书目"},"books":[{"id":"wind-in-the-willows","title":"柳林风声","englishTitle":"The Wind in the Willows","author":"Kenneth Grahame","grade":7,"term":"第一学期","intro":"春天，鼹鼠走出地下小屋，在河岸结识了河鼠、蟾蜍和獾先生。四位性格不同的朋友经历迷路、离家、追逐与重返家园。本导读沿原著十二章，带你在自然描写与冒险故事中，寻找友谊、归属感和为选择负责的证据。","themes":["友谊与互相照顾","家园与探索","自我约束与责任"],"guideNote":"本站原创简明导读；按原著十二章组织，改编读本的章节可能不同。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/289","characters":[{"name":"Mole（鼹鼠）","description":"好奇、敏感，珍惜自己的小屋。从接受河鼠帮助的新朋友，逐渐成长为能够照顾朋友、主动解决问题的伙伴。"},{"name":"Rat（河鼠）","description":"喜爱河流、划船和写诗，待朋友体贴。他也会忽略别人的心情或向往远方，需要学习倾听，并接受朋友的照顾。"},{"name":"Toad（蟾蜍）","description":"热情好客，喜欢新鲜事物，却常因自夸和冲动伤害自己与他人。他的成长要看行动、感谢与补偿，而不只看承诺。"},{"name":"Badger（獾先生）","description":"住在荒林深处，沉稳而可靠，为遇困的伙伴提供庇护。他帮助蟾蜍重返家园，也坚持要求蟾蜍承担应有的责任。"}],"sections":[{"id":"river-road","title":"河岸初遇与公路新奇","englishTitle":"The River and the Road","chapterRange":"原著第1—2章","reading":"Spring sunshine draws Mole away from cleaning his underground home. He reaches a river for the first time and meets Rat, who lives on its bank. Rat takes him boating and shares a picnic. Everything seems wonderful to Mole. He wants to row before he has learned how. He suddenly grabs the oars, and the boat turns over.\n\nRat pulls Mole safely from the water. Mole feels sorry for ignoring his advice. Rat chooses to forgive him and offers him a place to stay. He will teach Mole to swim and row. His patient help allows their friendship to grow, even after a foolish mistake.\n\nLater, they visit Toad, a friendly animal with a grand house and a new interest in travel. He persuades them to join a trip in a cart pulled by a horse. A fast car rushes past and frightens the horse. The cart falls into a ditch. Rat is angry about the danger, but Toad watches the car disappear with excitement. He soon orders one for himself, forgetting how quickly a wonderful journey became a frightening one.","summary":"鼹鼠初识河流，因急着划船而翻船；河鼠救起他、接受道歉，并愿意教他。随后，蟾蜍邀请朋友坐马车出游。疾驰的汽车吓到了马，马车翻入沟中，蟾蜍却只顾着迷恋汽车的速度。","vocabulary":[{"word":"bank","meaning":"河岸；此处不是“银行”","example":"They ate their picnic on the river bank."},{"word":"row","meaning":"划船","example":"Mole wants to learn how to row."},{"word":"forgive","meaning":"原谅","example":"Rat can forgive his friend after an honest apology."},{"word":"patient","meaning":"有耐心的","example":"A patient teacher gives learners time to practise."},{"word":"frighten","meaning":"使害怕","example":"The sudden noise may frighten the horse."},{"word":"excitement","meaning":"兴奋；激动","example":"Toad talks about the new car with excitement."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why does the boat turn over?","options":["A sudden flood hits the boat.","Mole takes the oars before he knows how to row.","Toad jumps into the boat.","A horse pulls the boat into the water."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第一段写鼹鼠还没有学会划船就突然抢过船桨，随后船翻了。翻船与他的贸然行动直接相连。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Rat offer Mole after rescuing him?","options":["A car and a map of the road.","A job cleaning Toad's house.","A horse for a trip on his own.","A place to stay and lessons in swimming and rowing."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第二段明确写河鼠邀请鼹鼠留下，并将教他游泳与划船。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer from Toad's reaction to the passing car?","options":["He notices its excitement more than its danger.","He has decided to stop travelling forever.","He is mainly worried about repairing the cart.","He already understands how to drive safely."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"马车刚因汽车经过而翻倒，蟾蜍却兴奋地望着汽车，还立刻订购一辆。这支持他更关注刺激、忽略危险的推断。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What does patient mean in the second paragraph?","options":["Always in a hurry to finish.","Unwilling to speak to anyone.","Willing to give someone time to learn.","Unable to move after an accident."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"河鼠愿意原谅鼹鼠，并继续教他游泳、划船，说明 patient 指愿意耐心帮助别人学习。","skill":"语境词义"},{"prompt":"Which idea best connects the events in this passage?","options":["The grandest house always has the best owner.","Friendship can help learning, while excitement can hide danger.","A new journey always ends better than an old one.","An accident means that friendship must end."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"前两段展示河鼠如何帮助犯错的鼹鼠学习，第三段展示蟾蜍如何因兴奋忽略风险，选项能兼顾两部分。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"鼹鼠翻船后愿意道歉，蟾蜍遇险后却立刻迷上汽车。请分别找一句英文证据，比较他们如何回应风险；哪些行动会影响下一次选择？","journalPrompt":"用50—70词写一次你急于尝试新事物的经历，也可以虚构。写清想尝试什么、收到什么提醒、后来如何调整，并尝试使用 patient 或 advice。"},{"id":"wild-wood","title":"荒林迷途与獾宅灯火","englishTitle":"Lost in the Wild Wood","chapterRange":"原著第3—4章","reading":"During winter, Mole wants to meet Badger, who lives deep in the Wild Wood. One afternoon, while Rat is asleep, Mole goes there alone. At first the trees seem interesting. As darkness grows, strange faces and running feet frighten him. He loses his way and hides inside a hollow tree, too tired to keep running.\n\nWhen Rat wakes, he notices that Mole is gone. He follows Mole's footprints towards the wood and calls his name as he searches. At last, a weak reply leads him to the tree. Rat's familiar voice comforts Mole. However, snow covers the paths, and both friends struggle to find their way home.\n\nMole hurts his leg on a metal object under the snow. Rat realizes that it is used to clean boots beside a door. He searches further, finds a doormat, and then discovers Badger's entrance. Badger welcomes the cold visitors, treats Mole's cut, and gives them supper and a warm bed. The next day, they meet two young hedgehogs who have also received shelter there. Before the friends leave, Badger shows them a tunnel to the edge of the wood.","summary":"鼹鼠独自进入荒林，迷路后躲进空心树。河鼠循着足迹与回应找到他，却和他一起被雪困住。门边刮泥器与门垫成为线索，指引他们找到獾宅。獾先生照料伤口、准备食宿，也为其他迷路的小动物提供庇护。","vocabulary":[{"word":"hollow","meaning":"空心的；内部有空处的","example":"The small animal hides inside a hollow tree."},{"word":"footprint","meaning":"脚印","example":"A footprint in the mud can show where someone went."},{"word":"reply","meaning":"回答；回应","example":"Rat hears a weak reply from the tree."},{"word":"entrance","meaning":"入口","example":"They clear the snow near the entrance."},{"word":"shelter","meaning":"庇护；可避风雨的地方","example":"Badger gives the visitors shelter from the snow."},{"word":"tunnel","meaning":"地道；隧道","example":"The tunnel leads to the edge of the wood."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Where does Mole hide when he becomes frightened?","options":["Under Rat's boat.","Inside a horse cart.","Inside a hollow tree.","Behind a cupboard in his own house."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第一段末尾明确说明，鼹鼠迷路后躲进了一棵空心树。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"How do the footprints help Rat?","options":["They show that Mole has gone towards the wood.","They show that Badger has visited the river.","They tell him when the snow will stop.","They lead directly into Toad's house."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段写河鼠沿鼹鼠通向树林的脚印前进，再通过呼喊寻找朋友。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer about Rat from the metal object scene?","options":["He gives up whenever the weather changes.","He already knows every entrance in the wood.","He thinks every object in the snow is dangerous.","He uses small clues to work out what may be nearby."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"河鼠由清理靴子的物件想到门，继续找到门垫和入口。这一连串行动说明他会根据线索逐步推断。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What does shelter mean in the last paragraph?","options":["A lesson about growing trees.","Protection and a safe place to stay.","A reason to leave home alone.","A tool for cutting wood."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"獾先生让寒冷、迷路的来客获得食物和温暖的休息处，两只小刺猬也得到同样的帮助，所以 shelter 指庇护。","skill":"语境词义"},{"prompt":"What do the rescue and Badger's welcome mainly show?","options":["A large house is useful only to its owner.","Being curious always brings an immediate reward.","Careful thinking and kindness can work together in trouble.","Friends must solve every problem without asking for help."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"河鼠凭线索寻找出路，獾先生以食宿和照料帮助来客；两部分共同体现解决困难既需要思考，也需要关怀。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"把“脚印—回应—门边物件—入口”中的两个线索与对应判断配成对。河鼠哪些行动体现了冷静思考？獾先生又用哪些行动让朋友重新安心？","journalPrompt":"以鼹鼠的口吻写50—70词日记，记录从害怕到安心的变化。至少提到一个找到你的线索和獾先生的一项照料，并用 finally 连接结尾。"},{"id":"home-choices","title":"旧家温暖与错误选择","englishTitle":"Home and Hard Choices","chapterRange":"原著第5—6章","reading":"One winter evening, Mole and Rat pass near Mole's old home. A familiar smell brings back his memories. Mole calls to Rat, but Rat is too far ahead to hear him clearly. Mole follows his friend, then begins to cry. When Rat understands, he turns back with him, although he is cold and hungry.\n\nMole worries that his small house is too poor for his guest. Rat praises it, lights a fire, and helps prepare supper. When field mice arrive to sing, the friends welcome them and arrange more food. Mole sees that he can love his old home and still enjoy the wider world. A place does not need to be grand to matter.\n\nLater, Badger, Rat, and Mole try to stop Toad's dangerous driving. They stay at his house and watch him because he refuses to give up cars. Toad pretends to be seriously ill and sends Rat to get help. Then he escapes. At an inn, he sees a car that belongs to someone else and drives away in it. He is caught and sent to prison. His friends' concern cannot replace the choices he must make himself.","summary":"熟悉的气味让鼹鼠想起旧家。河鼠理解他的难过后陪他返回，用赞美、炉火和晚餐表达尊重。另一边，三位朋友希望阻止蟾蜍危险驾驶；蟾蜍却装病脱身，又偷走汽车，最终被捕入狱。","vocabulary":[{"word":"familiar","meaning":"熟悉的","example":"A familiar smell reminds Mole of home."},{"word":"memory","meaning":"记忆；回忆","example":"A small object can bring back a happy memory."},{"word":"guest","meaning":"客人","example":"Mole wants his guest to feel comfortable."},{"word":"prepare","meaning":"准备","example":"The friends prepare supper together."},{"word":"refuse","meaning":"拒绝","example":"Toad may refuse good advice when he wants a new car."},{"word":"concern","meaning":"关心；担忧","example":"The friends show concern about his dangerous driving."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why does Rat first keep walking when Mole calls?","options":["He wants to sell Mole's old house.","He has promised never to visit Mole.","He is too far ahead to hear Mole clearly.","He is running after Toad's car."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第一段说明河鼠走在较远的前方，没有听清鼹鼠的呼唤；不能据此认定他故意拒绝朋友。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer about the value of Mole's old home?","options":["Its memories and personal meaning matter more than its size.","It matters only because it is bigger than Toad's house.","It has no value once Mole makes new friends.","Its value depends on how many cars it can hold."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"鼹鼠因气味想起旧家、流泪并回去，后来认识到可以同时珍爱小屋和外面的世界，说明价值来自回忆与归属。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What does refuses mean in the last paragraph?","options":["Forgets how to do something.","Learns to do something well.","Asks someone to repeat a message.","Does not agree to do something."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"朋友们希望蟾蜍放弃危险驾驶，他却不肯放弃汽车，因此 refuses 在这里表示“拒绝、不愿同意”。","skill":"语境词义"},{"prompt":"How does Toad get a chance to escape from his house?","options":["He waits until a field mouse opens his door.","He pretends to be ill and sends Rat to get help.","He follows a tunnel that Mole has built.","He offers to prepare supper for everyone."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第三段直接写蟾蜍假装重病，把河鼠支出去求助，随后逃走。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which statement best expresses a main idea of the passage?","options":["Old homes should always be left empty.","A friend must approve every exciting plan.","Friends can offer care, but each character still makes choices.","A person with a grand house does not need advice."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"河鼠的照顾帮助鼹鼠重新安心，三位朋友的关心却没能替蟾蜍作出正确选择，贯穿的是关怀与个人选择的关系。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"河鼠回头陪鼹鼠回家，与三位朋友阻止蟾蜍危险驾驶，都是怎样的帮助？每件事选一条文本证据，说明帮助方式为什么不同。","journalPrompt":"以鼹鼠口吻写50—70词的小屋日记，记录河鼠做的两件事，以及你的心情怎样变化。最后写一句小屋对你的意义，可以使用 familiar 或 memory。"},{"id":"dawn-escape","title":"黎明寻友与牢狱脱身","englishTitle":"A Search at Dawn and an Escape","chapterRange":"原著第7—8章","reading":"One summer night, Rat tells Mole that Otter's young son, Portly, has been missing for several days. His father is worried because the little animal cannot swim well. Mole does not want to wait at home. Together, he and Rat take a boat upstream and search the dark banks, hollow trees, and small waterways.\n\nNear dawn, they hear beautiful music. They follow it to an island, where a mysterious figure holds a set of pipes. Portly sleeps safely at his feet. The friends feel wonder and peace. Soon the figure disappears, and their memory of him fades. They take Portly back to his happy father. Their quiet search has ended in a reunion.\n\nElsewhere, Toad is unhappy in prison. The jailer's daughter helps him get clothes from her aunt, a washerwoman. This disguise lets him walk out of prison. At the station he discovers that he has left his money behind. A train driver offers him a ride. When another train pursues them, Toad admits who he is. The driver helps him get away into a wood. He is free for now, but still cold, hungry, and far from home.","summary":"河鼠和鼹鼠连夜寻找水獭的幼子 Portly，黎明时在神秘吹笛者身边找到安睡的小水獭，并送他与父亲团聚。蟾蜍则在狱卒女儿帮助下装扮成洗衣妇脱身，又得到火车司机相助；他暂时逃脱，却仍未回家。","vocabulary":[{"word":"missing","meaning":"失踪的；找不到的","example":"The missing child has been away for several days."},{"word":"dawn","meaning":"黎明","example":"The friends are still searching near dawn."},{"word":"pipes","meaning":"排箫；本段指吹奏乐器","example":"The beautiful sound comes from a set of pipes."},{"word":"fade","meaning":"逐渐消失；变淡","example":"The memory begins to fade like a dream."},{"word":"disguise","meaning":"伪装；乔装","example":"Toad wears different clothes as a disguise."},{"word":"pursue","meaning":"追赶；追踪","example":"Another train begins to pursue them."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why is Otter especially worried about Portly?","options":["Portly has taken Toad's new car.","Portly refuses to invite his friends home.","Portly is afraid of hearing music.","Portly has been missing and cannot swim well."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第一段同时给出两个原因：Portly 已失踪数日，而且游泳还不熟练。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Where do Rat and Mole find Portly?","options":["In a cupboard at Toad Hall.","On an island, at the feet of a mysterious figure.","On the train beside its driver.","In the jailer's daughter's room."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第二段写朋友们跟随音乐到达小岛，看到 Portly 安睡在神秘人物脚边。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Mole's decision to join the search suggest?","options":["He thinks Otter should solve every problem alone.","He wants to become the owner of the river.","He responds to another family's worry with practical effort.","He is certain that Portly is already home."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"鼹鼠听到消息后不愿留在家中等待，而是和河鼠划船搜寻河岸等处；他的关心落实为行动。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What does pursues mean in the last paragraph?","options":["Follows in order to catch.","Stops to offer food.","Turns into a different vehicle.","Waits quietly at home."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"另一列火车到来后，蟾蜍承认身份，司机又帮助他躲进树林。结合这段逃亡情境，pursues 表示追赶。","skill":"语境词义"},{"prompt":"Which statement connects the two story lines best?","options":["Both journeys begin with a stolen boat.","Both journeys end with everyone at Toad Hall.","Both stories show that money solves every difficulty.","Both stories show characters receiving help in trouble."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Portly 得到保护并由朋友送回，蟾蜍得到狱卒女儿和司机的帮助；“遇困时得到帮助”是两条线共有的内容。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"这一组故事中的帮助有哪些不同？分别用寻回 Portly、狱卒女儿帮助蟾蜍的一处细节，讨论接受帮助后可能还需承担什么责任。请把文本事实和你的判断分开。","journalPrompt":"从河鼠或鼹鼠的视角，用50—70词记下从担心到安心的变化。至少写出一项搜索行动，以及一处让你印象深刻的声音或景象。"},{"id":"restless-journeys","title":"远行诱惑与再度遇险","englishTitle":"Restless Hearts and Risky Journeys","chapterRange":"原著第9—10章","reading":"As the season changes, Rat notices birds preparing to leave. Then a travelling Sea Rat tells him about warm coasts, busy ports, and life aboard ships. Rat becomes restless. His familiar river no longer seems enough. He packs a bag and starts to leave, moving as if he were in a dream.\n\nMole sees that his friend is not thinking clearly and stops him. He stays nearby, listens, and talks about the coming seasons at home. Later, he brings Rat paper and a pencil. Rat slowly begins writing poetry again. Rat had once welcomed Mole and taught him to swim and row.\n\nMeanwhile, Toad gets a ride on a barge by pretending to be a washerwoman. His boast about washing creates trouble when he must actually do it. After an angry argument, the boatwoman throws him into the canal. Toad takes her horse and later sells it for food and money. Next, he gets a ride in a car and persuades the driver to let him drive. He speeds up and proudly reveals his identity. The journey ends in a pond. Running away again, he falls into the river and sees Rat at a hole in the bank.","summary":"海鼠的远行故事让河鼠坐立不安，几乎神情恍惚地离家。鼹鼠陪伴、倾听，并用纸笔帮助他重新写诗。蟾蜍则因吹嘘洗衣本领而露馅，偷卖船妇的马，又在驾车时失控。逃跑途中，他跌入河中，遇见河鼠。","vocabulary":[{"word":"restless","meaning":"不安的；难以安定下来的","example":"Rat feels restless after hearing stories of distant places."},{"word":"coast","meaning":"海岸","example":"Ships travel along the warm coast."},{"word":"aboard","meaning":"在船、飞机等交通工具上","example":"The Sea Rat enjoys life aboard ships."},{"word":"poetry","meaning":"诗歌","example":"Paper and a pencil help Rat return to writing poetry."},{"word":"boast","meaning":"自夸的话；吹嘘","example":"His boast about being an excellent washer is untrue."},{"word":"identity","meaning":"身份","example":"Toad reveals his identity while driving the car."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"What does the Sea Rat describe to Rat?","options":["Warm coasts, busy ports, and life on ships.","A new tunnel under Mole's house.","A plan to repair Toad's horse cart.","The best way to wash the boatwoman's clothes."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第一段写海鼠讲述温暖的海岸、繁忙的港口和船上生活，这些故事激起河鼠的远行念头。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Mole bring to help Rat return to an activity he enjoys?","options":["A car key and a driving coat.","A horse and a basket of food.","Paper and a pencil for writing poetry.","A new ticket for an ocean voyage."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第二段写鼹鼠带来纸和铅笔，随后河鼠又开始写诗。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What change in Mole and Rat's friendship is shown here?","options":["Mole decides he no longer needs any friends.","Rat now asks Mole to stop writing forever.","They can only be friends when both want to travel.","Mole, once helped by Rat, can now support Rat in return."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"鼹鼠的陪伴、倾听和送纸笔说明他在支持河鼠；末句也回顾河鼠曾教他游泳、划船。结合这些细节，可以看出他们能够互相照顾。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Why does Toad's boast about washing create a problem?","options":["The boatwoman asks him to build a new boat.","He is expected to do a job that he cannot actually do.","It causes Rat to throw away all his poems.","It makes the horse stop eating food."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第三段写蟾蜍吹嘘会洗衣，但真正需要洗时就露馅了。他夸口的本领与实际能力不符。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does restless mean when it describes Rat?","options":["Unable to feel settled and content where he is.","Certain that he wants to sleep all day.","Too cold to move his hands.","Satisfied that nothing should ever change."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"河鼠听完故事后觉得熟悉的河流不再足够，还收拾行李要走，说明 restless 指内心不安定、难以满足。","skill":"语境词义"}],"discussion":"这一阶段的两位角色都被新的生活吸引。找出河鼠停下来接受照顾、蟾蜍再次失去控制的证据。怎样区分探索的愿望和冲动的行动？","journalPrompt":"以朋友的口吻给河鼠或蟾蜍写50—70词留言：先回应对方的感受，再引用一个情节，提出一个可执行的建议，并说明理由。"},{"id":"return-responsibility","title":"重返蟾宫与学会担当","englishTitle":"Returning Home and Taking Responsibility","chapterRange":"原著第11—12章","reading":"Rat pulls Toad out of the river and gives him clean clothes. He also tells him firmly that his proud stories hide serious mistakes. Then Toad learns that a band of animals has taken over Toad Hall. He tries to return alone, but fails. At last, he agrees to listen to his friends.\n\nBadger knows a secret tunnel into the house. The friends plan to enter while the animals inside are holding a feast. Mole confuses the guards with a false story about an attack from outside. That night, the four friends move through the tunnel together. They rush into the dining hall, and the surprised occupiers flee. Toad gets his home back.\n\nAt the celebration, Toad first wants to give speeches and sing about himself. His friends object. He sings privately before the party, but behaves modestly with his guests and gives his friends credit. Later, he thanks the people who helped him escape. Badger still has to insist that he pay the boatwoman for her horse. Toad has begun to act differently, but some duties remain hard for him. His friends help him return home and also ask him to put right the harm he has done.","summary":"河鼠救起蟾蜍，也直言他的错误。得知家园被占后，蟾蜍独自行动失败，最终与朋友通过密道合作夺回蟾宫。他在宴会上克制自夸、感谢伙伴，却仍需獾先生督促赔付船妇的马钱；改变要落实在持续行动中。","vocabulary":[{"word":"secret","meaning":"秘密的","example":"Badger knows a secret way into the house."},{"word":"guard","meaning":"守卫","example":"The guard watches the entrance."},{"word":"feast","meaning":"宴会；盛宴","example":"The animals gather for a feast in the dining hall."},{"word":"modestly","meaning":"谦逊地；不自夸地","example":"Toad speaks modestly about his part in the plan."},{"word":"credit","meaning":"功劳；认可，常见于 give someone credit","example":"Toad gives his friends credit for their help."},{"word":"insist","meaning":"坚持要求","example":"Badger must insist that Toad pay for the horse."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"How do the four friends enter Toad Hall together?","options":["They arrive openly in a new motor car.","They go through a secret tunnel.","They climb down from a passing train.","They ask the guests to carry them inside."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第二段写四位朋友夜间一起经过密道进入屋内。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer from the way Toad finally gets his house back?","options":["The friends do not need to listen to one another.","Toad succeeds because he has the most money.","A loud speech is more useful than a plan.","Cooperation succeeds where his attempt alone has failed."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第一段写蟾蜍独自返回失败，第二段写朋友们分工计划、通过密道成功。比较两次行动，可推断合作是成功的重要因素。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Which action shows Toad behaving modestly at the party?","options":["He gives his friends credit for their help.","He orders every guest to sing about him.","He tells everyone that he worked alone.","He refuses to thank anyone who helped him."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第三段写蟾蜍在客人面前表现谦逊，并把功劳归给朋友，这与只歌颂自己不同。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does insist mean in the sentence about Badger and the horse?","options":["Forget that something has happened.","Ask a question without expecting an answer.","Keep saying firmly that something must be done.","Offer to hide a mistake from everyone."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"蟾蜍仍觉得有些责任难以承担，獾先生必须坚持要求他赔付马钱，因此 insist 表示坚决要求完成某事。","skill":"语境词义"},{"prompt":"Which sentence best describes Toad's change at the end?","options":["Getting his house back removes every responsibility.","He has learned that friends should praise every action.","He shows no change in how he treats his guests.","He acts more modestly but still needs help accepting some duties."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"蟾蜍愿意在宴会上克制自夸、承认朋友的功劳，却仍需被督促赔钱；两处证据共同表明改变已经开始但仍需努力。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"蟾蜍在宴会上把功劳归给朋友，赔付马钱时却还需要被督促。这两处证据怎样帮助你评价他的改变？再指出一处朋友既帮助他、又要求他承担责任的行动。","journalPrompt":"为蟾蜍写一份50—70词的行动日记：写出已经做到的一件事、仍需承担的一项责任和接下来怎样兑现。用 because 说明至少一个理由。"}]},{"id":"grimm-fairy-tales","title":"格林童话选","englishTitle":"Grimm's Fairy Tales","author":"格林兄弟（雅各布·格林、威廉·格林）","grade":7,"term":"第一学期","intro":"格林兄弟搜集整理的童话，把愿望、考验与选择放进奇幻故事。本导引以《灰姑娘》为示范，练习比较人物的外表与行动，并寻找判断善良、公平与勇气的文本证据。","themes":["善良与帮助","外表与行动","公平与选择"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页自选《灰姑娘》作为示范，不代表官方选篇目录。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/11027","characters":[{"name":"Cinderella 灰姑娘","description":"受到不公平对待的女孩；阅读时留意她的愿望、选择与行动。"},{"name":"The stepmother 继母","description":"给灰姑娘设置任务和限制的人物。"},{"name":"The birds 小鸟","description":"在格林故事中帮助灰姑娘的动物。"},{"name":"The prince 王子","description":"在宴会上遇见灰姑娘，后来借助鞋子寻找她。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Compare Appearance and Action","chapterRange":"选篇示范：《灰姑娘》（本站自选）","reading":"In this guide, we use Cinderella as one example from the Grimm stories. Cinderella lives with a family that makes her do hard work. Her stepsisters have fine clothes, while she wears old ones and sleeps near the ashes. Yet clothes do not tell us who is kind.\n\nWhen a feast is held at the palace, Cinderella wants to go. Her stepmother gives her difficult tasks. Birds help her, and she later appears at the feast in beautiful clothes. The prince wants to find the young woman he meets there. A lost shoe becomes an important clue.\n\nWhile you read, make two lists: what people look like and what they do. Do these lists tell the same story? Notice who offers help and who sets unfair rules. Then choose one action that shows Cinderella's character. Explain your choice with a detail from the story. Different editions may choose different Grimm tales, so check the contents of your school book before reading.","summary":"本页用《灰姑娘》示范如何阅读童话：了解她受到的限制与得到的帮助，再把人物外表和实际行动分开记录，用具体细节判断人物。阅读学校版本前，先核对选篇目录。","vocabulary":[{"word":"ashes","meaning":"灰烬","example":"The fire is out, but warm ashes remain."},{"word":"clue","meaning":"线索","example":"The small footprint is a clue to the mystery."},{"word":"unfair","meaning":"不公平的","example":"It is unfair to give one child all the work."},{"word":"character","meaning":"性格；人物","example":"Her kind actions show her character."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Which story is used as the example in this guide?","options":["Snow White","Cinderella","The Frog Prince","Rapunzel"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"首句明确说明，本导引用 Cinderella，即《灰姑娘》，作为格林童话的一个示范。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Who helps Cinderella with her difficulties in the passage?","options":["Birds","The prince's guards","Her stepsisters","A school friend"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段直接写到 Birds help her，帮助她的是小鸟。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer about Cinderella's place in the household?","options":["Her wishes control all the family rules.","She and her stepsisters share the work equally.","Her needs receive less respect than her stepsisters' needs.","She is free from household work."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"她承担辛苦家务、穿旧衣，而继姐妹穿华服；她想参加宴会时又被继母设置任务。这些细节共同说明，她的需要受到较少尊重。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What two lists does the guide ask readers to make?","options":["Foods and drinks","Places and dates","Wishes and dreams","People's appearance and actions"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"最后一段要求记录 what people look like 和 what they do，即外表与行动。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main purpose of this passage?","options":["To list every tale in a school edition","To introduce an example and a way to study characters","To explain how to make a shoe","To prove that all fairy tales have the same ending"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"文章先概述示范故事，再指导读者通过外表、行动和细节理解人物；它没有提供学校版本的完整目录。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"导引为什么把“穿什么”与“做什么”分成两张表？结合灰姑娘和继母各一项行动，讨论只看外表会造成什么误判。","journalPrompt":"用60—80词英文写一段人物观察：选灰姑娘或你读到的另一位童话人物，先写一个判断，再用两项行动支持它。"}]},{"id":"aesops-fables","title":"伊索寓言","englishTitle":"Aesop's Fables","author":"伊索（传统归名）","grade":7,"term":"第一学期","intro":"短小的寓言常让动物表现人的习惯，再用结果引出思考。本导引选《龟兔赛跑》练习梳理因果，区分天生优势与实际行动，也提醒读者用故事证据解释寓意，而不只背诵结论。","themes":["坚持与专注","自信与轻敌","行动与结果"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页自选《龟兔赛跑》作为示范，不代表官方选篇目录。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/11339","characters":[{"name":"The tortoise 乌龟","description":"速度较慢，但比赛过程中持续前进。"},{"name":"The hare 兔子","description":"跑得很快，却因轻视对手而在途中睡觉。"},{"name":"The fox 狐狸","description":"在参考故事中负责安排赛程并担任裁判。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Follow the Choices in a Race","chapterRange":"选篇示范：《龟兔赛跑》（本站自选）","reading":"A fable is a short story that invites us to think about our actions. This guide uses The Hare and the Tortoise as an example. A hare laughs at a tortoise because the tortoise moves slowly. The tortoise offers to race him. A fox helps arrange the race.\n\nAt first, the hare runs far ahead. He feels so sure of winning that he stops and falls asleep. The tortoise does not stop. Step by step, he reaches the finish before the hare. The faster animal loses because of a choice he makes during the race.\n\nAs you read, draw a line from each choice to its result. Do not write only that the hare is fast and the tortoise is slow. Ask how each animal uses the ability it has. This story values steady effort, but it does not say that speed is useless. Imagine the hare staying awake and running carefully. How might that change the result? Use the events to explain your answer.","summary":"导引以《龟兔赛跑》为例，把人物选择与比赛结果联系起来。重点是兔子因轻敌停止比赛、乌龟持续前进，而不是简单认为速度本身没有价值。","vocabulary":[{"word":"fable","meaning":"寓言","example":"We read a fable about two talking animals."},{"word":"arrange","meaning":"安排","example":"Our teacher will arrange the reading groups."},{"word":"ability","meaning":"能力","example":"Practice can help you develop your ability."},{"word":"steady","meaning":"持续而稳定的","example":"She makes steady progress by reading every day."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why does the hare laugh at the tortoise?","options":["The tortoise cannot find the road.","The tortoise is sleeping.","The tortoise moves slowly.","The tortoise refuses to race."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第一段说明兔子嘲笑乌龟，是因为乌龟行动缓慢。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does the hare do after running far ahead?","options":["He stops and falls asleep.","He helps the tortoise run.","He asks the fox to stop the race.","He goes straight to the finish."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段写到兔子领先后认为自己一定会赢，于是停下来睡着了。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which explanation best fits the result of the race?","options":["The fox carries the tortoise.","The tortoise becomes faster than every animal.","The race has no finish.","The hare wastes his advantage while the tortoise keeps moving."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"兔子本来领先，却选择睡觉；乌龟持续前进。把这两条证据联系起来，可以推断不同的选择改变了结果。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What does the guide ask readers to connect with a line?","options":["Each animal and its favourite food","Each choice and its result","Every place and its weather","Each word and its first letter"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第三段要求从 each choice 画线连到 its result，帮助梳理因果关系。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main reading lesson in this guide?","options":["A story can be understood by examining actions and consequences.","The quickest reader always understands best.","Every animal race ends in the same way.","A moral should be repeated without looking at events."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"全文围绕比赛中的选择、行动及其后果展开，并要求读者用事件解释寓意。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"“乌龟赢了，所以速度毫无用处”是否符合导引？引用兔子领先和后来睡觉这两条证据，解释你的判断。","journalPrompt":"用60—80词英文写一次练习经历，说明你做了什么、结果如何，以及下次准备怎样保持专注。"}]},{"id":"the-happy-prince","title":"快乐王子","englishTitle":"The Happy Prince","author":"奥斯卡·王尔德","grade":7,"term":"第一学期","intro":"一尊华美的王子雕像与一只准备远行的燕子，因看见城市中的困苦而相遇。导引帮助读者追踪他们一次次给予的选择，比较外在美与行动的价值，并思考关心他人需要怎样的付出。","themes":["同情与给予","外在美与价值","友谊与付出"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页围绕同名童话《快乐王子》；来源链接为包含该篇的原著故事集，不代表官方选篇目录。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/902","characters":[{"name":"The Happy Prince 快乐王子","description":"高处的雕像，看见城中苦难后希望帮助有需要的人。"},{"name":"The swallow 燕子","description":"本来准备飞往温暖地方，后来为王子传递帮助。"},{"name":"The seamstress 女裁缝","description":"王子和燕子帮助的人之一，需要照顾生病的孩子。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Look for the Value of Giving","chapterRange":"选篇示范：《快乐王子》（同名童话）","reading":"A beautiful statue stands high above a city. People call it the Happy Prince. From this high place, the Prince can see people who are hungry, cold, or worried. He cannot walk to them, but he wants to help.\n\nA swallow stops beside the statue on his way to a warmer country. The Prince asks the bird to carry a jewel to someone in need. The swallow agrees. More requests follow, and the bird stays. Together, they give away the jewels and the gold that make the statue beautiful. As winter comes, helping others becomes harder for the little bird.\n\nRead with a question in mind: does the Prince become less valuable when he looks less beautiful? Keep a record of what he gives, who receives it, and what the swallow must do. Notice that the two friends have different abilities. One can see the need; the other can travel. Their actions help us think about friendship and kindness. Look for evidence before deciding what the title means.","summary":"快乐王子看得到城中的困苦却无法移动，燕子则能把帮助送到需要的人身边。导引要求记录给予的对象与付出，并思考雕像失去金饰之后的价值。","vocabulary":[{"word":"statue","meaning":"雕像","example":"A stone statue stands near the gate."},{"word":"jewel","meaning":"宝石","example":"A bright jewel shines in the ring."},{"word":"request","meaning":"请求","example":"She listens carefully to her friend's request."},{"word":"valuable","meaning":"有价值的；贵重的","example":"Your time and help are valuable to us."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why can the Prince see so much of the city?","options":["He rides through it every day.","He reads every newspaper.","He lives beside every family.","His statue stands high above it."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"开头说明雕像立在城市高处，因此能看见城中饥寒或忧虑的人们。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Where is the swallow planning to go when he first stops?","options":["To a warmer country","To a mountain school","To an empty palace","To a colder island"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段说明燕子当时正在前往一个更温暖的国家。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Why do the Prince and the swallow make an effective team?","options":["They have exactly the same ability.","Their different abilities help turn concern into action.","They both refuse to leave the statue.","They want to keep all the jewels."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"王子看得到需要却不能走动，燕子能够飞行；两人的能力互相配合，使关心变成实际帮助。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Which item belongs in the reading record suggested by the guide?","options":["The price of every building","The number of birds in the world","What the Prince gives and who receives it","Every country on a map"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"最后一段要求记录王子给出什么、谁收到，以及燕子需要做什么。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which question best expresses the passage's main idea?","options":["How can a statue learn to fly?","Why should every bird collect gold?","Which jewel is the most expensive?","How can giving and friendship show true value?"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"全文把王子与燕子的帮助、友谊和付出联系到“价值”，并提出外表不再华美后是否仍有价值的问题。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"王子与燕子各自能做什么、又不能做什么？用导引中的两条信息说明，他们的合作怎样让帮助真正发生。","journalPrompt":"用60—80词英文描写一件有价值但不一定昂贵的事物或行动，联系王子或燕子的一次选择说明理由。"}]},{"id":"black-beauty","title":"黑骏马","englishTitle":"Black Beauty","author":"安娜·休厄尔","grade":7,"term":"第一学期","intro":"黑骏马用自己的声音讲述在不同主人身边生活和工作的经历。读者由此观察动物承受的辛劳，以及照料与粗暴对待带来的差别，练习从叙述者的感受寻找证据，思考责任和善意。","themes":["动物福利","责任与照料","换位思考"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/271","characters":[{"name":"Black Beauty 黑骏马","description":"以第一人称讲述自己经历的马，也是全书的观察者。"},{"name":"Ginger 姜儿","description":"黑骏马认识的一匹马，其经历帮助读者理解伤害与不信任。"},{"name":"Jerry Barker 杰里·巴克","description":"善待马匹的马车夫，关注工作、休息和照料。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Hear a Horse's Point of View","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"What would a working horse tell us if it could speak? In Black Beauty, a horse tells his own life story. As a young horse, he lives in a pleasant place. Later, he moves between owners and does different kinds of work. Some people care about his comfort. Others demand too much or hurt him through carelessness.\n\nBecause Beauty tells the story, readers learn how human actions feel to an animal. A tight rein or a long day may look ordinary to a person, but it can mean pain or exhaustion to a horse. Kind care includes food, rest, and attention to signs of trouble.\n\nWhile reading, make a record for each new home. Write what work Beauty does, how people treat him, and how he responds. Compare actions instead of judging an owner by a friendly name or a fine house. Ask whether someone notices the horse's needs. The story encourages us to see responsibility in small daily choices, not only in one brave rescue.","summary":"黑骏马的第一人称叙述，让读者从马的感受重新观察人的行为。导引建议按不同住所记录工作、待遇和反应，用日常照料的细节判断人物是否尽到了责任。","vocabulary":[{"word":"owner","meaning":"主人；拥有者","example":"The dog's owner brings fresh water."},{"word":"comfort","meaning":"舒适；安适","example":"A dry bed adds to the animal's comfort."},{"word":"exhaustion","meaning":"精疲力竭","example":"After the long walk, he rested because of exhaustion."},{"word":"responsibility","meaning":"责任","example":"Caring for a pet is a daily responsibility."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Who tells the life story in Black Beauty?","options":["A horse","A railway worker","A sailor","A king"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第一段直接说明 a horse tells his own life story，即马讲述自己的经历。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which kind of care is mentioned in the passage?","options":["Giving the horse a famous name","Painting the stable gold","Providing food, rest, and attention","Making the horse work every night"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第二段指出善意照料包括食物、休息，以及关注异常迹象。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Why might the horse's narration change a reader's view of a long working day?","options":["The horse knows every owner's thoughts.","The horse can describe suffering that people may overlook.","The horse believes all work is enjoyable.","The horse thinks houses are more important than rest."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"导引说人觉得普通的长时间工作，可能意味着马的疼痛或疲惫，因此动物视角能揭示人容易忽略的感受。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What should readers record for each new home?","options":["Only the colour of the house","Only the owner's name","The number of windows and doors","Beauty's work, treatment, and response"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"最后一段要求记录黑骏马做什么工作、人如何对待他，以及他怎样反应。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main focus of this guide?","options":["Winning a horse race","Understanding care and responsibility through an animal's experience","Learning how to buy a large house","Remembering the dates of every journey"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"导引通过动物叙述、不同待遇及日常照料，帮助读者理解换位思考与责任。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"为什么一座漂亮的房子不能证明主人善待马匹？从导引中选出两项更有说服力的判断依据。","journalPrompt":"用60—80词英文从一种动物的视角写一段日记，描述一个人的具体行为，以及这个行为带来的感受和需要。"}]},{"id":"arabian-nights","title":"一千零一夜","englishTitle":"The Arabian Nights","author":"传统故事集（参考安德鲁·朗选编本）","grade":8,"term":"第一学期","intro":"这部流传中不断汇集的故事集，常以一个故事引出另一个故事。本页自选辛巴达第一次航海作为示范，观察意外、应变与他人帮助如何共同推动情节，并学习区分人物见闻和自己的推断。","themes":["冒险与应变","帮助与机遇","故事中的故事"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页自选“辛巴达第一次航海”作为示范，不代表官方选篇目录；来源为安德鲁·朗选编的传统故事集。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/128","characters":[{"name":"Sindbad 辛巴达","description":"讲述自己航海经历的商人，在示范篇目中遭遇意外并努力求生。"},{"name":"Hindbad 脚夫","description":"听辛巴达讲述经历的人；不同译本的人名写法可能不同。"},{"name":"The captain 船长","description":"第一次航海中的船长，后来与辛巴达重逢。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Separate Surprise, Action, and Help","chapterRange":"选篇示范：辛巴达第一次航海（本站自选）","reading":"The Arabian Nights brings together many traditional stories. This guide chooses Sindbad's first voyage as one example; your school edition may contain a different selection. Sindbad tells a visitor about the dangers behind his comfortable life. His account becomes a story inside another story.\n\nOn his first voyage, Sindbad travels with merchants. One day, the sailors land on what seems to be a small island. They light a fire, and the ground suddenly moves. Their island is actually a great whale. When it dives, Sindbad is left in the sea, holding a piece of wood. He eventually reaches land, where other people help him. Later, he meets his ship again and recovers his goods.\n\nWhile reading, make three columns: surprise, response, and help. The moving island belongs in the first column. Holding the wood belongs in the second. Support from people he meets belongs in the third. This prevents us from explaining survival through courage alone. Chance and help also matter.\n\nNotice what Sindbad knew at each moment. He did not know the island was a whale when he landed. Ask how new information changes his choices, and separate your own guesses from details the storyteller gives.","summary":"导引选择辛巴达第一次航海，展示故事中套故事的结构。阅读时把意外、个人应对和外部帮助分别记录，既关注勇气，也看到机遇和合作对脱险的作用。","vocabulary":[{"word":"voyage","meaning":"航海；航行","example":"The long voyage began at a busy port."},{"word":"merchant","meaning":"商人","example":"The merchant carried cloth to another town."},{"word":"recover","meaning":"找回；恢复","example":"They hope to recover the missing bags."},{"word":"response","meaning":"回应；应对","example":"Her response to the problem was calm and practical."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"What does the small island turn out to be?","options":["A wooden ship","A great whale","A floating palace","A sleeping bird"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第二段明确揭示：他们以为的小岛其实是一头巨鲸。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Sindbad hold when he is left in the sea?","options":["A gold box","A merchant's coat","A piece of wood","A rope from the ship"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第二段写到辛巴达被留在海里时抓住一块木头。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"A reader says, 'Sindbad survives entirely through his own strength.' Which detail most strongly challenges that claim?","options":["People help him after he reaches land.","He tells a visitor about his life.","He travels with goods to sell.","He first thinks that he sees a small island."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"“完全靠自己”排除了外部帮助，但靠岸后有人提供帮助，构成直接反证。人物出海贸易或讲故事不能反驳这项说法。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Which item belongs in the 'response' column?","options":["The island starts moving.","The island is a whale.","People offer support on land.","Sindbad holds on to the wood."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第三段用 holding the wood 直接示范 response，即辛巴达自己的应对行动。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main purpose of this guide?","options":["To provide the official contents of every edition","To prove that every unusual story is a true report","To introduce a selected adventure and a way to examine its causes","To give instructions for starting a sea business"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"全文以本站选择的航海故事为例，指导读者分析意外、应对、帮助及信息变化，而非公布学校目录。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"假如只用“辛巴达很勇敢”解释他脱险，会遗漏哪些证据？从导引中找出一项个人行动和两项外部因素。","journalPrompt":"用80—100词英文写一段航海日志，明确区分“我当时看到了什么”“我做了什么”与“后来才知道什么”。"}]},{"id":"robin-hood","title":"罗宾汉","englishTitle":"Robin Hood","author":"英国传统传说（参考霍华德·派尔整理本）","grade":8,"term":"第一学期","intro":"罗宾汉故事由长期流传的传说发展而来，不同版本的事件和人物安排并不完全相同。本导引参考派尔整理本，观察森林伙伴的合作、对失败的态度和援助行为，用具体行动讨论勇气与公平。","themes":["勇气与谦逊","同伴与合作","公平与责任"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。罗宾汉属于传统传说；本页参考霍华德·派尔整理本，不代表官方指定版本或章节安排。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/964","characters":[{"name":"Robin Hood 罗宾汉","description":"舍伍德森林中的传说人物，本导引关注他的应变与待人方式。"},{"name":"Little John 小约翰","description":"在桥上与罗宾汉交手，后来成为伙伴。"},{"name":"The Sheriff of Nottingham 诺丁汉郡长","description":"追捕罗宾汉及其伙伴的官员，是多则故事中的对手。"},{"name":"Sir Richard of the Lea 理查德爵士","description":"在参考故事中得到罗宾汉帮助、面对债务困难的骑士。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Judge Courage Through Choices","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"Robin Hood belongs to a long tradition of stories, so different books do not always tell the same adventures. This guide draws on Howard Pyle's version. Robin lives with a band of companions in Sherwood Forest, while the Sheriff of Nottingham tries to capture him.\n\nOne useful scene takes place on a narrow bridge. Robin meets a stranger, and neither man wants to step aside. They fight with wooden staffs, and Robin falls into the water. After losing, he can laugh at himself and welcome the stranger as a companion. The newcomer becomes known as Little John. In another adventure, Robin helps a knight who is struggling with a debt.\n\nThese events offer different kinds of evidence about a leader. Skill with a weapon is only one part of the picture. His response to defeat and his treatment of someone in difficulty also matter. While reading, record the problem, Robin's choice, and the effect on other people.\n\nDo his companions simply follow orders, or do their abilities change what happens? Look for a scene that supports your answer. You can admire courage while still asking whether a particular action is fair. Explain your judgment through the event, rather than through the hero's reputation alone.","summary":"导引参考派尔整理本，用桥上相遇和援助骑士两个片段，引导读者从应对失败、接纳伙伴及帮助他人等行动判断罗宾汉，而不只依据英雄名声。","vocabulary":[{"word":"companion","meaning":"同伴","example":"Each traveller should check that their companion is nearby."},{"word":"capture","meaning":"抓住；俘获","example":"The guards plan to capture the thief."},{"word":"defeat","meaning":"失败；战败","example":"He learns something useful from his defeat."},{"word":"reputation","meaning":"名声；声誉","example":"She has a reputation for keeping her promises."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Which version does this guide draw on?","options":["A new film script","A newspaper report","A school timetable","Howard Pyle's version"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第一段直接说明，本导引参考 Howard Pyle 的版本。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What happens to Robin during the fight on the bridge?","options":["He falls into the water.","He loses his way in the forest.","He captures the sheriff.","He hides behind a tree."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段说明两人用木杖交手后，罗宾汉落入水中。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Robin's welcome to the stranger suggest?","options":["He can only respect people who always lose.","He is unable to work with anyone.","He can recognize another person's ability after his own defeat.","He thinks friendship requires no choices."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"罗宾汉虽然输掉交手，仍能笑对自己并接纳对方；这支持他能够承认他人本领的推断。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What three things should readers record?","options":["Names, birthdays, and favourite meals","The problem, Robin's choice, and its effect on others","The weather, clothes, and weapon prices","Only the order of the chapter titles"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第三段要求记录问题、罗宾汉的选择，以及对其他人的影响。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which idea best describes the guide's main message?","options":["A famous hero never makes a questionable choice.","Winning a fight is the only sign of leadership.","Every version must contain exactly the same scenes.","A leader's actions and their effects deserve careful judgment."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"导引要求把武艺、面对失败的态度、待人方式和行动影响综合起来，用证据判断领导者。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"桥上相遇这一情节为何既能表现竞争，也能表现合作的起点？结合罗宾汉落水后的两个行动说明。","journalPrompt":"用80—100词英文写一段对罗宾汉的评价：提出一个关于勇气或公平的判断，用一项具体事件支持，并保留一个值得继续追问的问题。"}]},{"id":"peter-pan","title":"彼得·潘","englishTitle":"Peter Pan","author":"J. M. 巴里","grade":8,"term":"第一学期","intro":"彼得带温迪和弟弟们飞往梦幻岛，冒险的快乐也伴随着危险、牵挂和选择。导引通过比较彼得与温迪对成长和家的态度，帮助读者追踪愿望的变化，思考自由、责任与记忆之间的联系。","themes":["成长与选择","想象与冒险","家庭与责任"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。英文原著参考巴里的小说《Peter and Wendy》，常以《Peter Pan》为书名出版。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/16","characters":[{"name":"Peter Pan 彼得·潘","description":"能够飞行、不愿长大的男孩，带领孩子们前往梦幻岛。"},{"name":"Wendy Darling 温迪·达林","description":"喜爱故事和冒险，也牵挂家人并逐渐作出自己的选择。"},{"name":"Tinker Bell 小叮当","description":"陪伴彼得的仙子，其情绪和行动会影响故事发展。"},{"name":"Captain Hook 胡克船长","description":"梦幻岛上的海盗船长，与彼得及伙伴发生冲突。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Follow the Wish to Grow","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"Imagine leaving your bedroom through the window and flying towards an island of adventures. Peter Pan offers Wendy Darling and her brothers this possibility. Peter can fly, and he does not want to grow up. In Neverland, they meet the Lost Boys, fairies, and pirates, including Captain Hook.\n\nAt first, the journey seems full of freedom. There are games, stories, and exciting discoveries. Yet danger and responsibility enter the adventure too. Wendy cares about the children and remembers the family waiting at home. Her wish to return shows that loving an adventure does not remove every other need. Peter's wish to remain a boy leads him towards a different choice.\n\nAs you read, keep separate records for Peter and Wendy. What does each want at the beginning? Which events strengthen or change those wishes? Use their decisions as evidence instead of assuming that they feel the same because they travel together.\n\nThe idea of never growing up can sound delightful, but the story also raises questions about memory and lasting relationships. Notice who remembers, who forgets, and who waits. At the end of your reading, explain one gain and one cost of a character's choice. More than one thoughtful judgment is possible when it is supported by details.","summary":"导引把彼得与温迪的愿望分开追踪：共同冒险并不意味着两人对成长、家庭与责任有相同看法。阅读时用决定、记忆和等待等细节解释选择带来的收获与代价。","vocabulary":[{"word":"possibility","meaning":"可能性","example":"The open door offers the possibility of a new start."},{"word":"responsibility","meaning":"责任","example":"The team shares responsibility for the younger children."},{"word":"strengthen","meaning":"加强；使更坚定","example":"Her experience may strengthen her wish to help."},{"word":"relationship","meaning":"关系","example":"Regular letters help them maintain their relationship."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Where does Peter take Wendy and her brothers?","options":["A city beneath the sea","A railway station","Neverland","A desert market"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第一段说明孩子们飞往 Neverland，即梦幻岛。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Peter not want to do?","options":["Meet the Lost Boys","Grow up","Listen to any story","Leave an island"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第一段直接写到 Peter does not want to grow up。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which statement is Wendy most likely to agree with, based on this passage?","options":["A return home can be a meaningful choice after an adventure.","Enjoying adventures means forgetting every family relationship.","Everyone should make the same decision as Peter.","A person must dislike a place before deciding to leave it."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"温迪享受冒险，却也关心孩子、记得家人并希望回家；综合这些细节，可以推断她会把回家视为有意义的选择，而非否定全部冒险。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Why should readers keep separate records for Peter and Wendy?","options":["Only one of them appears in the story.","Their names are easy to confuse.","They are travelling to different islands at the start.","Their wishes and decisions may develop differently."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第三段要求分别记录两人起初的愿望及其变化，并提醒不能因同行就假设感受相同。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main purpose of this passage?","options":["To teach readers how to fly","To explore choices about adventure, growth, and relationships","To list every pirate in all editions","To prove that there is only one possible judgment of Peter"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"全文通过人物愿望、成长态度和对家人的牵挂，指导读者有证据地讨论选择。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"温迪想回家，是否就意味着她不喜欢冒险？结合导引中“自由的乐趣”与“家庭的牵挂”两方面信息回答。","journalPrompt":"用80—100词英文给彼得或温迪写一封不发送的信，讨论其选择的一项收获与一项代价，并引用一个故事细节。"}]},{"id":"the-railway-children","title":"铁路少年","englishTitle":"The Railway Children","author":"伊迪丝·内斯比特","grade":8,"term":"第一学期","intro":"父亲突然不在身边，三个孩子随母亲搬到铁路附近，在改变的生活中结识朋友、面对困难。导引关注他们如何观察他人的需要并共同采取行动，也引导读者从零散线索理解家庭的秘密。","themes":["家庭与希望","观察与行动","善意与合作"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1874","characters":[{"name":"Roberta（Bobbie）罗伯塔（博比）","description":"三个孩子中的姐姐，关心家人与他人的感受。"},{"name":"Peter 彼得","description":"对铁路充满好奇，参与伙伴间的计划和行动。"},{"name":"Phyllis 菲莉丝","description":"最小的妹妹，与哥哥姐姐一同经历乡间生活。"},{"name":"Mother 母亲","description":"在家庭突变后照顾孩子，并通过写作维持生活。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Notice How Small Actions Connect","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"Roberta, Peter, and Phyllis begin the story in a comfortable London home. After their father suddenly goes away, they move with their mother to a house near a railway. Money is limited, and the children do not understand all the reasons for this change. Trains become an important part of their new daily life.\n\nThe children wave to an older passenger and make friends with railway workers. These small meetings gradually create connections. During one adventure, they discover that fallen earth and rocks are blocking the railway line. They use red clothing to warn an approaching train. Their success depends on noticing a danger, understanding a signal, and working together.\n\nThe book also develops a mystery around the children's absent father. Readers learn some things slowly, just as the children do. Keep a question list, and add the evidence that becomes available. A worry is not the same as a confirmed fact.\n\nWhen reading an act of kindness, look beyond the immediate result. Does it build trust that matters later? Record who offers help and who receives it. The same person may take both roles at different times. This makes the story useful for thinking about a community: people become connected through attention, effort, and care.","summary":"导引从家庭变化、铁路伙伴和警示列车的事件入手，强调观察、合作与互助。阅读父亲缺席之谜时，应随新线索更新问题，把担忧和已确认的事实分开。","vocabulary":[{"word":"limited","meaning":"有限的","example":"We have limited time, so we need a clear plan."},{"word":"signal","meaning":"信号","example":"The light is a signal for the driver."},{"word":"evidence","meaning":"证据","example":"One detail gives us evidence for the answer."},{"word":"community","meaning":"社区；共同体","example":"A library can bring people in a community together."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Where do the children move after their father goes away?","options":["To a ship in a harbour","To a house near a railway","To an island palace","To a school inside a forest"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第一段说明他们和母亲搬到铁路附近的房子。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is blocking the railway line in the adventure described?","options":["A group of sleeping horses","An empty passenger train","A collection of old books","Fallen earth and rocks"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第二段明确说塌落的泥土和石块阻塞了铁路线。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does the train-warning episode suggest about the children's role in their new community?","options":["They can contribute only after learning the truth about their father.","Their friendly waves are enough to solve any problem.","They can make a valuable contribution by applying knowledge together.","They need to be railway employees before they can help anyone."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"孩子们发现阻塞、理解红色信号并合作警示列车；这些行动帮助了乘客，因此可以推断，他们能够凭知识与合作为共同生活作出贡献。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"How should readers handle the mystery about the father?","options":["Keep questions and update them with new evidence.","Treat every worry as a confirmed fact.","Ignore all later information.","Decide the answer from the first sentence alone."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第三段建议保留问题清单，并随着证据增加更新理解，同时区分担忧和事实。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which statement best describes the main idea of the guide?","options":["Railways matter only because trains move quickly.","Family stories never contain mysteries.","Only adults can help a community.","Careful attention and mutual help connect people through change."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"全文把家庭变化中的观察、合作、善意和人际信任联系起来，展现互助如何形成共同生活。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"导引为什么说同一个人可能先帮助别人、后来接受帮助？用铁路旁的交往和“建立信任”的信息解释这种关系。","journalPrompt":"用80—100词英文记录一次互助经历：说明最初的小行动、对方的反应，以及它是否改变了你们之后的关系。"}]},{"id":"white-fang","title":"白牙","englishTitle":"White Fang","author":"杰克·伦敦","grade":8,"term":"第一学期","intro":"白牙在严酷环境与不同人的对待中学习生存，也经历从戒备到信任的变化。导引引导读者把环境、人的行为与白牙的反应联系起来，理解伤害的后果，以及耐心照料为何需要持续的行动。","themes":["环境与成长","伤害与信任","照料与改变"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/910","characters":[{"name":"White Fang 白牙","description":"具有狼和犬血统的动物，经历让他逐渐学会戒备，也重新学习信任。"},{"name":"Kiche 吉赤","description":"白牙的母亲，在他早期学习生存的经历中十分重要。"},{"name":"Beauty Smith 比尤蒂·史密斯","description":"以残酷方式利用白牙进行斗犬的人。"},{"name":"Weedon Scott 威登·斯科特","description":"救助白牙，并通过耐心与稳定照料建立信任的人。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Trace the Growth of Trust","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"White Fang grows up in a cold northern world where finding food and avoiding danger are daily tasks. He has both wolf and dog ancestry. As he moves through different surroundings, his behaviour changes with what he experiences. Hunger, attacks, and harsh treatment teach him to be watchful and ready to defend himself.\n\nA cruel owner, Beauty Smith, uses White Fang in fights. Later, Weedon Scott rescues him and begins to offer a different kind of human contact. Scott's patience does not erase the past in a single moment. Trust develops through repeated experiences of care. An approaching hand can gradually mean something different from the threat White Fang once expected.\n\nWhile reading, build a chain with three parts: situation, treatment, and response. If White Fang reacts fiercely, look back for evidence about what he has learned to expect. This helps you explain behaviour without treating every harmful action as acceptable.\n\nAlso notice small changes. Does White Fang approach, withdraw, or wait? Such actions can reveal more than a simple label like brave or bad. Compare two moments when a person comes near him. What stays the same, and what changes? Your answer should connect his response to specific experiences rather than assume that trust appears instantly.","summary":"白牙的防备与变化都和经历有关。导引建议记录处境、待遇和反应之间的联系，通过靠近、退避、等待等小动作观察信任如何形成，同时保留对伤害行为的判断。","vocabulary":[{"word":"ancestry","meaning":"血统；祖先背景","example":"The animal has both wolf and dog ancestry."},{"word":"defend","meaning":"保护；防御","example":"The mother bird tries to defend her nest."},{"word":"patience","meaning":"耐心","example":"Learning to trust may require time and patience."},{"word":"withdraw","meaning":"退开；撤回","example":"The frightened animal may withdraw into a quiet corner."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"What are two daily challenges in White Fang's early world?","options":["Finding food and avoiding danger","Buying books and choosing clothes","Learning to sail and building a ship","Collecting jewels and guarding a palace"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第一段开头把寻找食物和避免危险列为白牙每天面对的任务。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Who rescues White Fang from the cruel situation described?","options":["Captain Hook","Little John","Weedon Scott","The Sheriff of Nottingham"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第二段说明 Weedon Scott 救助白牙，并开始给予不同的接触和照料。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Why might White Fang initially see an approaching hand as a threat?","options":["He has never met a person.","Past harsh treatment has shaped what he expects.","Every hand is carrying food.","Scott has already removed every fear."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"前文说伤害经历使白牙保持防御，后来又提到手曾意味着威胁；把两处信息联系起来可知，过去经历影响了他的预期。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Which chain does the guide suggest readers build?","options":["Title, author, and publication price","Colour, size, and age","Beginning, page number, and cover","Situation, treatment, and response"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第三段直接提出三部分记录链：处境、受到的对待和反应。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main reading focus of the passage?","options":["Choosing the strongest animal in every fight","Showing that one kind act changes everything immediately","Understanding how experience and repeated care shape trust","Proving that harmful actions never need to be questioned"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"导引强调经历塑造反应，信任需要反复的照料体验，并要求通过小动作和前后对比寻找证据。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"“斯科特救了白牙，所以白牙立刻完全信任人类”有什么证据不足？引用导引中关于过去经历和反复照料的信息回答。","journalPrompt":"用80—100词英文比较白牙前后两次面对人的反应，分别写出动作、可能的原因，以及你依据的具体细节。"}]},{"id":"twenty-thousand-leagues","title":"海底两万里","englishTitle":"Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea","author":"儒勒·凡尔纳","grade":9,"term":"第一学期","intro":"阿龙纳斯教授与伙伴发现，神秘海怪背后竟是一艘潜艇。奇异海洋世界带来求知的兴奋，也暴露自由受限的处境。导引围绕不同人物的愿望与证据，讨论科学探索、技术力量和人的选择。","themes":["探索与知识","自由与权力","技术与责任"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/164","characters":[{"name":"Professor Aronnax 阿龙纳斯教授","description":"研究自然的学者，也是讲述海底经历的主要叙述者。"},{"name":"Captain Nemo 尼摩船长","description":"掌管鹦鹉螺号，以自己的规则支配船上的生活。"},{"name":"Conseil 康塞尔","description":"阿龙纳斯的随行伙伴，冷静细致，热心观察和分类。"},{"name":"Ned Land 尼德·兰","description":"经验丰富的捕鲸手，十分看重离开潜艇、恢复自由的机会。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Explore Wonder, Freedom, and Power","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"An unknown object at sea is believed to be a dangerous creature. Professor Aronnax joins the search, but the mystery leads him, Conseil, and Ned Land to an extraordinary discovery: the object is a submarine. Captain Nemo commands this vessel, the Nautilus, which can carry its passengers into a world few people have seen.\n\nFor Aronnax, the voyage offers an astonishing opportunity to study ocean life. He observes creatures, landscapes, and the workings of the submarine. Ned Land, however, pays close attention to chances of escape. Their different interests create tension. The same journey can be an exciting scientific experience and a loss of freedom, because the visitors cannot simply choose to leave.\n\nAs you read, keep two linked records. In the first, note what Aronnax discovers and why it attracts him. In the second, record decisions made by Nemo and the effects on other people. Compare the narrator's admiration with the practical limits placed on his life.\n\nThe submarine is more than a setting for adventures. It gives its captain knowledge, mobility, and control. Ask how these forms of power are used in a particular scene. Who makes the decision, who benefits, and who bears the cost? A careful answer can recognize the wonder of exploration while examining the responsibilities that accompany it.","summary":"导引把海洋探索的吸引力与旅客无法自由离开的处境并置，要求分别记录阿龙纳斯的发现、尼摩的决定及其影响，分析技术带来的知识、控制力和责任。","vocabulary":[{"word":"submarine","meaning":"潜艇","example":"The submarine travels below the surface of the sea."},{"word":"tension","meaning":"紧张关系；矛盾","example":"Their different aims create tension within the group."},{"word":"admiration","meaning":"钦佩；赞赏","example":"Her admiration grows as she studies the invention."},{"word":"mobility","meaning":"移动能力；行动自由度","example":"A reliable vehicle gives the explorers greater mobility."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"What is the mysterious object discovered by Aronnax and his companions?","options":["A submarine","A sea castle","A giant sailing bird","A railway tunnel"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第一段明确说明，被当作危险生物的神秘物体实际上是一艘潜艇。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What interests Ned Land especially during the journey?","options":["The price of Nemo's books","The colour of every sea creature","The history of each meal","Opportunities to escape"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第二段指出尼德·兰特别关注逃离潜艇的机会。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Why might Aronnax and Ned evaluate an offer to remain aboard differently?","options":["They have already agreed that leaving is impossible forever.","Ned has no interest in decisions about his own life.","They give different weight to scientific discovery and personal freedom.","Aronnax has learned nothing that interests him during the voyage."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"阿龙纳斯被海洋研究机会吸引，尼德特别关注逃离；由两人的关注点可以推断，他们衡量继续留船的利弊时，会给予知识与自由不同权重。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What should go in the second reading record?","options":["Only the names of ocean creatures","Nemo's decisions and their effects on other people","Every word that begins with the letter N","Only the dates when meals are served"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第三段要求第二份记录关注尼摩作出的决定，以及这些决定对别人的影响。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which idea best captures the guide's central focus?","options":["A scientific journey should be judged only by its discoveries.","A powerful invention always makes every person equally free.","All passengers understand the voyage in exactly the same way.","Scientific wonder can be examined together with freedom and responsibility."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"全文既关注探索与发现，也追问自由、控制力及其责任，要求综合这些方面评价具体情节。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"如果阿龙纳斯赞叹海底奇观，是否就能证明他认可尼摩的所有决定？结合导引中“研究机会”与“无法自由离开”的证据说明。","journalPrompt":"用100—120词英文评价小说中的一项技术或一次决定，说明谁获益、谁承担代价，并用两项情节细节支持你的判断。"}]},{"id":"treasure-island","title":"金银岛","englishTitle":"Treasure Island","author":"罗伯特·路易斯·史蒂文森","grade":9,"term":"第一学期","intro":"一张藏宝图把吉姆带上海上旅程，也把他带入真假难辨的人际关系。导引关注西尔弗的言行、吉姆获得信息的时机和冒险中的选择，训练读者修正初步判断，讨论信任、贪欲与成长。","themes":["信任与证据","贪欲与选择","冒险与成长"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/120","characters":[{"name":"Jim Hawkins 吉姆·霍金斯","description":"卷入寻宝冒险的少年，讲述全书的大部分经历。"},{"name":"Long John Silver 高个子约翰·西尔弗","description":"经验丰富、善于交际的船上厨师，同时参与海盗夺船计划。"},{"name":"Dr Livesey 利弗西医生","description":"参与寻宝的成年人，在危机中提供判断与帮助。"},{"name":"Captain Smollett 斯莫列特船长","description":"负责航行的船长，重视纪律并警惕船上的风险。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Revise a Judgment When Evidence Changes","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"A map of buried treasure draws young Jim Hawkins into a voyage on the Hispaniola. The ship's cook, Long John Silver, appears friendly and capable. He knows how to talk to people and has plenty of experience at sea. For a young traveller, he can seem like someone worth trusting.\n\nJim's understanding changes when he overhears plans for a mutiny, a rebellion against the ship's leaders. Silver is involved. The map may show where treasure lies, but it cannot tell Jim whose promises are reliable. Later, Silver's actions remain complicated: he can help Jim while also protecting his own chances of survival.\n\nKeep an evidence table as you read. For each important character, record a promise, an action, and the situation in which it occurs. If your judgment changes, explain which new detail caused the change. Revising an opinion can show careful reading.\n\nJim tells much of the story, so readers often receive information when he receives it. Ask what he knows before a decision and what becomes clear only afterwards. This helps distinguish a reasonable choice under uncertainty from a choice that looks easy after the result is known.\n\nThe adventure also connects greed with danger. As the search develops, compare the value characters place on wealth, loyalty, and human life. Support your conclusions with choices they actually make.","summary":"导引把藏宝图与人物信任区分开来，要求读者记录承诺、行动和处境，随新证据修正判断。分析吉姆的决定时，还应区分他当时知道的信息与事后才揭晓的结果。","vocabulary":[{"word":"mutiny","meaning":"船员哗变；反叛","example":"The captain hears rumours of a mutiny."},{"word":"reliable","meaning":"可信赖的；可靠的","example":"A reliable witness explains exactly what she saw."},{"word":"revise","meaning":"修正；修改","example":"We may revise our opinion when new evidence appears."},{"word":"uncertainty","meaning":"不确定性","example":"The team must make a decision under uncertainty."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"What draws Jim into the voyage?","options":["An invitation to teach at a school","A map of buried treasure","A plan to study horses","A letter from a time traveller"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第一段说明，一张埋藏财宝的地图使吉姆踏上旅程。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What does Jim learn by overhearing the plan?","options":["The treasure has already been given away.","Silver has never been to sea.","The ship is a submarine.","Silver is involved in a mutiny."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第二段说明吉姆听到哗变计划，并发现西尔弗参与其中。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can readers infer from Silver's friendly manner and hidden plan?","options":["A pleasant manner alone is insufficient evidence of trustworthiness.","Experienced sailors always tell the truth.","A treasure map reveals everyone's motives.","Jim should never change his first opinion."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"西尔弗表面友好能干，却参与夺船计划；两条证据说明友善表现本身不足以证明可信。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What question helps readers judge Jim's decisions fairly?","options":["How much does his coat cost?","Which chapter title is the shortest?","What information does he have before he decides?","Can the reader already guess the final page?"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第四段要求辨别吉姆决策前知道什么，以及后来才知道什么，避免仅凭事后结果评价选择。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main purpose of the passage?","options":["To provide the fastest route to a real treasure","To guide evidence-based judgments about trust, choices, and motives","To prove that every character wants the same thing","To explain how to cook meals on a ship"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"导引以吉姆与西尔弗为重点，训练读者依据言行和信息变化，分析信任、决定与动机。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"为什么“读者后来知道的结果”不应直接当作“吉姆当时知道的事实”？选导引中的夺船线索，说明信息出现的时机会怎样改变评价。","journalPrompt":"用100—120词英文写一次人物判断的修正：先写你的初步看法，再说明哪条新证据改变了它，以及哪些问题仍未解决。"}]},{"id":"the-merchant-of-venice","title":"威尼斯商人","englishTitle":"The Merchant of Venice","author":"威廉·莎士比亚","grade":9,"term":"第一学期","intro":"一份危险的借款契约把友谊、复仇和法庭争论连在一起。导引帮助读者辨认人物的请求、选择及后果，同时认真审视剧中的反犹偏见和强制改宗，讨论仁慈是否真正平等地给予每个人。","themes":["仁慈与公正","偏见与权力","承诺与后果"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页按戏剧原作展开批判性阅读，人物的行为不代表任何宗教群体。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1515","characters":[{"name":"Antonio 安东尼奥","description":"为帮助朋友而借款的商人，也是危险契约约定的承担者。"},{"name":"Shylock 夏洛克","description":"犹太放贷人，遭受宗教侮辱，也作出索取残酷惩罚的选择。"},{"name":"Portia 鲍西娅","description":"以法律专家身份乔装进入法庭，通过解释契约改变局面。"},{"name":"Bassanio 巴萨尼奥","description":"安东尼奥的朋友，希望获得资金去追求鲍西娅。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Ask Who Receives Mercy","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"Antonio borrows money from Shylock to help his friend Bassanio, who hopes to marry Portia. Their bond, or written agreement, contains a terrible condition: if the debt is not repaid, Shylock may claim a pound of Antonio's flesh. When repayment fails, a dispute over money becomes a threat to a human life.\n\nPortia enters the court disguised as a legal expert. She asks for mercy and then examines the exact words of the bond. Her argument prevents Shylock from taking Antonio's blood along with the flesh. Antonio is saved, but the outcome also requires Shylock to become a Christian.\n\nRead this result carefully. Shylock has suffered insults because he is Jewish, and he chooses a cruel form of revenge. Both the prejudice directed at him and his own actions deserve attention. One character's choices cannot justify a judgment about an entire religious group.\n\nFor each courtroom speech, record the speaker, the request, and the effect. Who appeals to mercy? Who has the power to grant it? Who is forced to give something up? A victory for one character does not settle every question about fairness.\n\nAs a play, the work gives meaning through dialogue and performance. Imagine how a pause or a change of tone could affect a speech. Support your interpretation with the words and consequences of the scene.","summary":"导引概述危险契约与法庭转折，既关注夏洛克的复仇选择，也正视他受到的反犹侮辱和强制改宗。阅读时记录谁请求仁慈、谁掌握权力、谁承担代价，避免用单个人物概括宗教群体。","vocabulary":[{"word":"bond","meaning":"契约；书面约定","example":"The characters disagree about the meaning of the bond."},{"word":"mercy","meaning":"仁慈；宽恕","example":"She asks the person in power to show mercy."},{"word":"prejudice","meaning":"偏见","example":"Prejudice can prevent people from judging others fairly."},{"word":"interpretation","meaning":"理解；阐释","example":"The actor's tone supports a different interpretation of the speech."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Why does Antonio borrow money?","options":["To build a submarine","To buy a railway station","To help Bassanio","To finance a voyage into the future"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第一段明确说明安东尼奥借钱是为了帮助朋友巴萨尼奥。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"How does Portia enter the courtroom?","options":["Disguised as a legal expert","As the captain of a ship","As Antonio's servant","Disguised as a railway worker"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第二段直接说明鲍西娅乔装成法律专家进入法庭。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What else happens in the outcome, besides Antonio being saved?","options":["Every character leaves the city immediately.","The bond is never discussed.","Shylock becomes the judge.","Shylock is required to become a Christian."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第二段在安东尼奥获救后，明确指出夏洛克被要求改信基督教。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Why does the guide say a victory does not settle every question about fairness?","options":["The play has no dialogue.","Saving one person can occur alongside an imposed loss for another.","No one in the play asks for mercy.","Every person receives an identical outcome."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"安东尼奥获救与夏洛克被迫改宗同时发生；联系这两点可以推断，一方获胜并不自动说明每个人都得到公正对待。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What is the guide's central approach to the play?","options":["Judge a whole religion by one character.","Ignore the consequences once the court speaks.","Examine words, prejudice, power, and the distribution of mercy.","Treat every request for revenge as fair."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"导引要求同时分析台词、偏见、决定权和仁慈的实际后果，并明确反对用人物行为概括宗教群体。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"法庭上谈论仁慈的人，是否也把仁慈给予了每一个人？依据导引中安东尼奥和夏洛克各自的结果，提出一个有证据的判断。","journalPrompt":"用100—120词英文写一段法庭场景评论，分别说明一项被避免的伤害和一项被施加的损失，再讨论你如何理解仁慈与公正。"}]},{"id":"robinson-crusoe","title":"鲁滨逊漂流记","englishTitle":"Robinson Crusoe","author":"丹尼尔·笛福","grade":9,"term":"第一学期","intro":"鲁滨逊在海难后学习利用物资、安排劳动并记录生活，展现出坚韧和实践能力。导引也关注他如何命名、支配和描述他人，引导读者把生存智慧与作品中的奴役、殖民观念一并纳入讨论。","themes":["生存与实践","叙述与证据","殖民与权力"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。本页依据原作讨论生存技能、叙述视角与殖民关系；不同节写本可能省略相关情节。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/521","characters":[{"name":"Robinson Crusoe 鲁滨逊·克鲁索","description":"海难幸存者与第一人称叙述者，组织岛上生活，也以自己的观念评价他人。"},{"name":"Friday 星期五","description":"鲁滨逊救下并重新命名的人，拥有自己的知识、经历和行动能力。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Read Survival and Power Together","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"After a shipwreck, Robinson Crusoe must organize a life on an island. He brings useful supplies from the damaged ship, builds shelter, grows food, and learns through repeated attempts. His records of work and daily needs make survival a series of practical problems. Progress often depends on patience and using available resources carefully.\n\nCrusoe also tells the story in his own voice. Readers receive his fears, beliefs, and judgments along with descriptions of events. This makes it useful to ask two questions: what happens, and how does Crusoe explain it?\n\nThe book includes difficult questions about power. Before the shipwreck, Crusoe joins a voyage intended to obtain enslaved people. Later, he rescues a man whom he names Friday and teaches to call him Master. These details connect the adventure with slavery and colonial attitudes. Friday has knowledge and abilities of his own, although the narrative is controlled mainly by Crusoe's voice.\n\nKeep one record of the narrator's practical achievements and another of how he treats and describes other people. Admiring his persistence does not require accepting every judgment he makes. Ask who chooses a name, who gives orders, and whose account is missing.\n\nFor a closer reading, select one event and separate its observable actions from the narrator's opinion. Then explain how hearing Friday's perspective might change the questions you would ask.","summary":"导引既关注鲁滨逊的实践能力，也要求审视他参与奴隶贸易航行、给星期五命名并确立主从称呼的行为。通过分开事件与叙述者评价，读者能思考作品中的权力关系和缺席的声音。","vocabulary":[{"word":"shelter","meaning":"遮蔽处；住所","example":"They build a shelter before the heavy rain begins."},{"word":"resource","meaning":"资源；可利用的材料","example":"Fresh water is a vital resource on the island."},{"word":"persistence","meaning":"坚持；坚韧","example":"Her persistence helps her improve after several failed attempts."},{"word":"perspective","meaning":"视角；观点","example":"The same event may look different from another person's perspective."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"Where does Crusoe obtain useful supplies after the shipwreck?","options":["From a railway shop","From a time machine","From a forest palace","From the damaged ship"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第一段说明鲁滨逊从受损的船上取来有用物资。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which detail in the guide shows Crusoe establishing authority over Friday?","options":["He teaches Friday to call him Master.","He gives Friday control of the whole narrative.","He asks Friday to choose Crusoe's new name.","He stops making any decisions on the island."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第三段指出鲁滨逊给对方取名星期五，并教他称自己为 Master，这直接表现主从关系。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is a reasonable inference about reading only Crusoe's account?","options":["It guarantees that every person's view is equally represented.","Some of Friday's own understanding may remain unheard.","It makes every opinion an observable fact.","It removes the need to ask about power."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"导引说叙述主要由鲁滨逊的声音控制，并追问谁的讲述缺席，因此星期五的部分理解可能没有得到充分表达。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"What two records does the guide recommend?","options":["Weather reports and ship prices","Only dates and place names","Crusoe's practical achievements and his treatment of other people","Friday's clothing and the island's colours"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"第四段明确要求分别记录鲁滨逊的实践成就，以及他如何对待和描述别人。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the central purpose of this passage?","options":["To present every judgment by Crusoe as unquestionable","To argue that patience has no role in survival","To teach readers how to take control of other people","To examine survival skills together with narration and unequal power"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"全文同时介绍生存实践、第一人称叙述和奴役、殖民关系，要求读者有证据地综合分析。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"为什么欣赏鲁滨逊的坚持，不必同时认同他对星期五的所有安排？分别引用一项生存行动和一项权力关系的证据。","journalPrompt":"用100—120词英文分析一个涉及星期五的场景：先写文本明确呈现的行动，再提出星期五可能追问的问题。将你的想象清楚标为想象，不当作原文事实。"}]},{"id":"the-time-machine","title":"时间机器","englishTitle":"The Time Machine","author":"H. G. 威尔斯","grade":9,"term":"第一学期","intro":"时间旅行者来到遥远未来，最初的美好印象很快受到新发现的挑战。导引关注他如何提出并修改解释，引导读者区分观察与假设，同时思考不同群体的劳动、生活条件和社会不平等。","themes":["观察与假设","未来与进步","劳动与不平等"],"guideNote":"本站原创阅读导引；请配合学校选用的版本阅读。","sourceUrl":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/35","characters":[{"name":"The Time Traveller 时间旅行者","description":"发明时间机器并讲述未来见闻的人，随着发现不断调整解释。"},{"name":"Weena 维娜","description":"时间旅行者在未来结识的埃洛伊人，与他建立情感联系。"},{"name":"The Eloi 埃洛伊人","description":"生活在地表的未来群体，旅行者起初从他们的生活推测社会状况。"},{"name":"The Morlocks 莫洛克人","description":"与地下空间和机器联系紧密的未来群体，其出现改变旅行者的判断。"}],"sections":[{"id":"reading-guide","title":"读前导引与理解","englishTitle":"Test an Explanation Against New Evidence","chapterRange":"整本书导引","reading":"A man known as the Time Traveller builds a machine that carries him far into the future. He reaches the year 802,701 and encounters a world that first seems gentle and comfortable. The Eloi live above ground. Their lives appear easy, and he begins to form an explanation of how this society developed.\n\nNew discoveries make that first explanation less convincing. The Morlocks live below ground, where machinery continues to operate. The Time Traveller's machine disappears, and fears associated with darkness suggest that life is more dangerous than he first imagined. He changes his ideas as he learns more, but his explanations remain attempts to understand unfamiliar evidence.\n\nRead with a notebook divided into observation and interpretation. Seeing underground machinery is an observation. Explaining the complete history of the people who use it requires further reasoning. Whenever the traveller changes a theory, identify the detail that makes him reconsider it.\n\nHis ideas about the two groups connect the adventure with questions about unequal work and comfort. Can a society measure progress only through pleasant surroundings or an easy life for some people? Consider whose labour remains hidden from the first view.\n\nThe future in this story is imagined, so treat it as an invitation to question human choices. Choose one of the traveller's claims, examine the supporting evidence, and decide how certain he can reasonably be.","summary":"导引把未来冒险转化为证据训练：区分看到的现象和对社会来历的解释，追踪旅行者如何根据新发现修改假设，并思考地表舒适生活与地下劳动之间的联系。","vocabulary":[{"word":"encounter","meaning":"遇见；遭遇","example":"The explorers encounter an unfamiliar landscape."},{"word":"observation","meaning":"观察；观察所得","example":"We should record the observation before explaining it."},{"word":"interpretation","meaning":"解释；理解","example":"Two readers may offer different interpretations of the same clue."},{"word":"reconsider","meaning":"重新考虑","example":"New evidence makes her reconsider the first answer."}],"questions":[{"prompt":"How does the Time Traveller reach the distant future?","options":["By following a treasure map","By using a machine he builds","By boarding the Nautilus","By walking through a railway tunnel"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"第一段说明时间旅行者制造了一台能够把他带到遥远未来的机器。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"Which description matches the passage?","options":["Both groups live only on ships.","The Eloi operate every underground machine in the passage.","The Morlocks live in the traveller's original home.","The Eloi live above ground, and the Morlocks live below ground."],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"第一、二段分别指出埃洛伊人生活在地表，莫洛克人生活在地下。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What can we infer about the limits of the traveller's early conclusions?","options":["He already possesses a complete history of both groups.","His pleasant first impression proves there is no hidden danger.","He has seen only part of this world and may miss important connections.","He can identify every cause without examining new discoveries."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"起初他只看到地表似乎舒适的生活，地下机器、时间机器失踪和黑暗中的危险后来才出现；由这些信息差可推断，早期结论建立在不完整观察上。","skill":"证据推断"},{"prompt":"Which example does the guide classify as an observation?","options":["Seeing machinery underground","Knowing the complete history of the society","Proving that all future life is comfortable","Deciding that every unfamiliar group has the same aim"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"第三段明确把看到地下机器作为 observation；对完整社会历史的解释则需要进一步推理。","skill":"细节理解"},{"prompt":"What is the main focus of this reading guide?","options":["Predicting the exact technology people will build in 802,701","Testing explanations and questioning how a society defines progress","Listing every machine used in modern cities","Proving that the first impression of a place is always correct"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"全文训练区分观察与解释、依据新证据修正假设，并通过隐藏的劳动和舒适生活追问社会进步。","skill":"主旨理解"}],"discussion":"“我看见地下有机器”与“我已经知道这个社会的完整历史”为什么不是同一层次的判断？结合导引说明中间还需要什么证据。","journalPrompt":"用100—120词英文提出一个关于未来社会的假设，写出两项支持它的观察，再说明哪种新证据会让你修改这一假设。"}]}]};
